      "plan_variable": "pplan:vars/concept/euclidean_normalizer",
      "summary": "Euclidean normalizer (Cheshire group): The normalizer of a space group in the Euclidean group. The translation part is the allowed-origin group T', and the linear part is the set of metric-holohedry rotations that conjugate the space group to itself. Both are derived from the operators. Inversion (det -1) maps a chiral molecule to its mirror image. The affine normalizer is not computed.",
      "agent": "agentsg-kg-builder/0.1 (Claude Fable 5.1, Cowork session, 2026-09-30)"
    },
