        "sha256": "51df66f7799d7f3daf27bc0a9fe0524b06c8c95b49b45283e47f88d305cc33da"
      },
      "plan_variable": "pplan:vars/concept/sorted_linear_key",
      "summary": "Sorted linear search key: The archive search key sort(p_ij / sqrt(T)), with T the sum of the six Selling conorms, in \u00e5ngstr\u00f6m. One key per lattice, a rearrangement lower bound on the labelled distance, Lipschitz in the metric, and linear in the cell edges. A cube of edge a has key (0, 0, 0, a/\u221a3, a/\u221a3, a/\u221a3), and an isotropic edge change \u0394a moves the key by \u0394a. Floored and soft-threshold maps are noise models for serial frames, not this key. Stored columns r0..r5 keep the square-root products.",
      "agent": "agentsg-kg-builder/0.1 (Claude Fable 5.1, Cowork session, 2026-09-30)"
    },
